3️⃣ ForkJoinPool & Work Stealing

Used for parallel processing of large tasks.

Java introduced ForkJoinPool for divide-and-conquer algorithms.

Example tasks:

Big array processing
Parallel sorting
Data analytics
Machine learning preprocessing
Concept

Task is split into smaller subtasks.

Big Task
   ↓
Split into smaller tasks
   ↓
Parallel execution
   ↓
Combine results
Work Stealing Algorithm

Each thread has its own task queue.

Example:

Thread1 queue → 10 tasks
Thread2 queue → 2 tasks
Thread3 queue → empty

Thread3 will steal tasks from Thread1.

This ensures CPU utilization stays high.

Example
ForkJoinPool pool = new ForkJoinPool();

pool.submit(() -> {
    IntStream.range(1, 1000)
        .parallel()
        .forEach(System.out::println);
});
